      "name": "ReadFileWithBuffer",
      "signature": "uint ReadFileWithBuffer(Smack * pSmack, byte * pBuffer, uint cbBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Reads bytes from a file with optional ring buffer support and rate throttling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Record start time using timeGetTime() for rate limiting\n  2. Check if buffering is disabled (pSmack+0x450 == 0)\n     a. If disabled: perform single ReadFile() call and return\n     b. If enabled: proceed with buffered read algorithm\n  3. Buffered read loop:\n     a. Copy available bytes from ring buffer to output (pSmack+0x460)\n     b. Update buffer pointers and wrap if needed (pSmack+0x458)\n     c. If more bytes needed and buffer empty: refill via ReadFile()\n     d. For large reads (>0x1000): read directly in 0x4000 (16KB) chunks\n     e. Call progress callback if registered (g_pfnProgressCallback)\n  4. Rate throttling (if pSmack+0x4c4 != 0):\n     a. Calculate target elapsed time: (bytesRead * 1000) / throttleRate\n     b. Spin-wait on timeGetTime() until target time reached\n  5. Update total bytes read counter (pSmack+0x46c)\n  6. Update elapsed time counter (pSmack+0x470)\n  7. Return total bytes successfully read\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack  Pointer to Smack file handle structure (see layout below)\n  pBuffer Destination buffer to receive read data\n  cbBytes Number of bytes to read\n\nReturns:\n  Number of bytes successfully read and placed in pBuffer\n  May be less than requested if end-of-file reached or read error occurs\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Direct mode (pSmack+0x450 == 0): single ReadFile with no buffering\n  - Circular buffer: when read pointer (pSmack+0x458) reaches end (pSmack+0x454), wraps to buffer start (pSmack+0x450)\n  - Large reads (>0x1000): bypass buffer and read directly in 16KB chunks\n  - Rate limiting: if throttle rate set (pSmack+0x4c4), delays to maintain target bytes/second\n  - Progress callbacks: calls g_pfnProgressCallback if g_dwProgressCallbackCount != 0\n  - EOF handling: sets error flag at pSmack+0x3a8 if short read detected\n\nSmack Structure Layout (partial):\nOffset | Size | Field              | Type    | Description\n-------|------|-------------------|---------|--------------------------------------------\n0x3b0  |  4   | hFile             | HANDLE  | Windows file handle for ReadFile operations\n0x450  |  4   | pbBufferStart     | DWORD   | Ring buffer base address (0 = no buffer)\n0x454  |  4   | pbBufferEnd       | DWORD   | Ring buffer end boundary address\n0x458  |  4   | pbBufferCurrent   | DWORD   | Current read position in ring buffer\n0x45c  |  4   | pbBufferReset     | DWORD   | Reset position for buffer refill\n0x460  |  4   | cbBufferAvailable | DWORD   | Number of bytes available in buffer\n0x464  |  4   | cbBufferWrap      | DWORD   | Size for buffer wrap calculation\n0x468  |  8   | qwBytesRead       | QWORD   | Total bytes read (statistics)\n0x46c  |  4   | dwTotalBytesRead  | DWORD   | Cumulative byte counter\n0x470  |  4   | dwElapsedTime     | DWORD   | Cumulative elapsed time in milliseconds\n0x4c4  |  4   | dwThrottleRate    | DWORD   | Target throughput (bytes/sec, 0=no limit)\n0x3a8  |  4   | dwErrorFlags      | DWORD   | Error/status flags (bit 0 = EOF/error)\n",
