      "name": "ReadSmackFrame",
      "signature": "uint ReadSmackFrame(Smack * pSmack)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Reads the next Smack video frame data from file into the buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check status flags at offset 0x390 for paused state (bit 0x200)\n  2. If paused, return 0 immediately\n  3. Store current buffer (offset 0x3d0) to previous buffer (offset 0x3d4)\n  4. Get frame index from offset 0x374\n  5. Look up frame size from frame table (offset 0x3dc) using frame index\n  6. Store frame size to offset 0x378\n  7. Call ReadFileWithBuffer to read frame data into buffer\n  8. Return bytes read\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack (Smack*) - Pointer to Smack context structure\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Number of bytes read, or 0 if paused/error\n\nStructure Layout (accessed offsets):\n  Offset | Size | Field              | Type   | Description\n  0x374  | 4    | dwFrameIndex       | uint   | Current frame index\n  0x378  | 4    | dwFrameSize        | uint   | Current frame size in bytes\n  0x390  | 4    | dwFlags            | uint   | Status flags (0x200 = paused)\n  0x3d0  | 4    | pCurrentBuffer     | byte*  | Current read buffer pointer\n  0x3d4  | 4    | pPreviousBuffer    | byte*  | Previous buffer pointer\n  0x3dc  | 4    | pFrameTable        | uint*  | Pointer to frame size table\n\nCallers:\n  _SmackOpen@12 - Initial frame read during file open\n  _SmackNextFrame@4 - Reads next frame during playback",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:a57732b2f37b9a4bcade104eed0884ce",
