      "name": "FindFirstSetBitAndClear",
      "signature": "byte FindFirstSetBitAndClear(dword * pMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "byte",
      "comment": "Finds the first set bit in a bitmask and clears it.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize bit index to 0, bit mask to 0x2000 (bit 13)\n  2. Loop through up to 7 bits:\n     a. Test if current bit mask matches any bits in *pMask\n     b. If match found: clear the bit from *pMask and return bit index\n     c. Increment bit index, shift bit mask left (multiply by 2)\n  3. If no bits found after 7 iterations, return 0xff (not found)\n\nParameters:\n  pMask - pointer to 32-bit bitmask value; bits are tested from 0x2000\n          (bit 13) through 0x4000000 (bit 26). Matched bit is cleared.\n\nReturns:\n  0-6: bit index of first set bit found (0x2000 through 0x4000000)\n  0xff: no bits found in range",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c40146b28c4500b00dbb5befa35d7792",
