      "name": "GetInterpolatedValue",
      "signature": "int GetInterpolatedValue(int nAnimationPtr)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Calculates interpolated animation value based on elapsed time.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Retrieve current animation state pointer from pAnimation\n  2. Get current system time via timeGetTime()\n  3. Calculate elapsed time since animation start\n  4. If elapsed time < duration: interpolate based on progress ratio\n     Interpolated = (MaxValue * ElapsedTime) / Duration\n  5. If elapsed time >= duration: return maximum value\n  6. Add base value offset to interpolated result\n\nParameters:\n  pAnimation - Pointer to animation structure containing timing and value fields\n    Offset 0x6c: Base value (initial offset)\n    Offset 0x70: Start time (from timeGetTime())\n    Offset 0x74: Duration in milliseconds\n    Offset 0x78: Maximum value\n\nReturns:\n  int - Interpolated value between base value and (base value + max value)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
