      "name": "ProcessSmackBufferList",
      "signature": "void ProcessSmackBufferList(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes the Smack buffer list by copying audio data, initializing audio buffers, and updating timing information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Iterate through linked list of Smack buffers starting at g_pSmackBufferListHead\n  2. For each buffer, check if data is ready to copy (offset 0x10 <= size at offset 0x44 or at offset 0x68)\n  3. Initialize audio state (0x8000000) via callback\n  4. Copy audio data using MemoryCopyRegions, adjust data size\n  5. If not mono (offset 0x50 == 0), XOR each byte with 0x80 (audio data inversion)\n  6. Set up audio format structure: sample rate, channels, bit depth\n  7. Call audio processing callback for prepared buffer\n  8. Update timing: record start time (timeGetTime) or accumulate samples if already running\n  9. Move to next buffer in linked list (offset 0x3c)\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - modifies global buffer list in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty buffer list (g_pSmackBufferListHead == NULL): immediate return\n  - Mono audio (offset 0x50 != 0): skip XOR inversion loop\n  - First buffer in timing sequence: initialize start time\n  - Timing overflow: reset timer, accumulate samples\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_pSmackBufferListHead - pointer to head of Smack buffer linked list\n  g_pfnInitializeCallback - audio init callback (offset 0x10015d34)\n  g_pfnProcessSmackStream - stream processor callback (offset 0x10015d54)\n  timeGetTime - Windows timer function\n  MemoryCopyRegions - buffer copy function",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:a1d1e4f6bf483b5a5b8343940a26aa6c",
