      "name": "GetAudioStreamPosition",
      "signature": "uint GetAudioStreamPosition(int pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Retrieves the current playback position of an audio stream with interpolation\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Update audio processing timers (ProcessAudioStreamTimer call)\n  2. Calculate initial position from stream offset 0x70 (current sample position)\n  3. If stream is paused (offset 0x60 == 0), use current position directly\n  4. If stream is playing, add difference of write_position(0x74) - start_offset(0x44)\n  5. Clamp negative positions to 0\n  6. Get current system time from timeGetTime() for interpolation\n  7. If calculated position equals last_reported_position (offset 0x84):\n     - Apply time-based interpolation using playback_rate (offset 0x14)\n     - Interpolation formula: last_pos + (current_time - last_time) * rate / 1000\n     - Clamp result to maximum stream position (offset 0x70)\n  8. Otherwise, update cached position (offset 0x84) and timestamp (offset 0x88)\n  9. Return max_reported_position (offset 0x8c), updating if current is higher\n\nParameters:\n  pStream [ESP+0x4] - Pointer to audio stream structure\n    Offset 0x14 - Playback rate (samples/millisecond)\n    Offset 0x44 - Start offset in stream buffer\n    Offset 0x60 - Pause flag (0=paused, nonzero=playing)\n    Offset 0x70 - Current sample position in stream\n    Offset 0x74 - Write position in buffer\n    Offset 0x84 - Last reported position (cached)\n    Offset 0x88 - Last time-based interpolation timestamp\n    Offset 0x8c - Maximum position ever returned\n\nReturns:\n  EAX - Current audio position (uint, in samples or time units)\n        Always >= previous return value (monotonically increasing)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Position interpolation prevents stuttering between actual updates\n  - Clamping to max prevents backtracking in playback position\n  - Paused streams return fixed position from offset 0x70\n  - Supports variable playback rates via offset 0x14 field",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:a2261bf973b846a63ab12819cf46eb99",
