      "name": "InitializeDirectSoundWindow",
      "signature": "BOOL InitializeDirectSoundWindow(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "BOOL",
      "comment": "Initializes DirectSound with an appropriate window handle for audio output.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Call DirectSoundCreate to create the DirectSound object\n  2. If creation fails and debug mode enabled (g_bDebugAudio == 0x01):\n     - Convert error code to string using itoa (radix 0x0A)\n     - Output error message via OutputDebugStringA\n     - Return FALSE (AL = 0)\n  3. If g_hDirectSoundHWND is set, use it directly\n  4. Otherwise, find a suitable window handle:\n     a. Get top-level window via GetTopWindow(NULL)\n     b. Get current process ID via GetCurrentProcessId\n     c. Enumerate windows with GetWindow(hwnd, GW_HWNDNEXT (0x02))\n     d. For each window, check if it belongs to current process via GetWindowThreadProcessId\n     e. If matching window found, use it\n     f. If no match, fallback to GetActiveWindow\n  5. Set g_bAudioInitialized = 1\n  6. Call _SmackSoundSetDirectSoundHWND@4 with the window handle\n  7. Set g_dwAudioResetFlag = 1\n  8. Return TRUE (AL = 1)\n\n  Parameters:\n    None - uses ZF flag as implicit input for conditional jump at entry\n\n  Returns:\n    BOOL - TRUE (1) on success, FALSE (0) on DirectSound creation failure\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Entry point checks ZF flag - if not zero, jumps directly to success return\n    - Uses g_pfnDirectSoundCreate function pointer loaded from dsound.dll\n    - Window enumeration uses GW_HWNDNEXT (0x02) to iterate siblings",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:b5623d40cc9d350f0a063193506dcf22",
