      "name": "BlitMergeWithColorKey",
      "signature": "void BlitMergeWithColorKey(byte * pDest, int nDestPitch, byte * pSrc, int nSrcPitch, uint dwWidth, int nHeight, byte byColorKey, byte * pFallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Blits source pixels to destination with color key transparency and fallback substitution\n\nAlgorithm\n  1. Outer loop: Iterate over nHeight rows\n  2. SIMD check: If DetectSIMDCapabilities() >= 2 and dwWidth >= 8, use MMX path\n  3. MMX path (processes 8 bytes per iteration):\n     a. Broadcast byColorKey to all 8 bytes of MM0 using PUNPCKLWD/PUNPCKLDQ\n     b. Load 8 bytes from pSrc into MM1\n     c. Load 8 bytes from pFallback into MM2\n     d. PCMPEQB MM1, MM0 - creates 0xFF mask where bytes match color key, 0x00 elsewhere\n     e. PAND MM2, MM1 - keeps fallback bytes where mask is 0xFF (color key match)\n     f. PANDN MM1, MM3 - inverts mask and keeps source bytes where mask was 0x00\n     g. POR MM1, MM2 - combines fallback and source bytes\n     h. MOVQ [pDest], MM1 - writes result to destination\n     i. Advance pointers by 8, decrement loop counter\n  4. Scalar remainder: Process remaining 0-7 bytes (dwWidth & 7)\n     a. For each byte: if (*pSrc == byColorKey) *pDest = *pFallback; else *pDest = *pSrc\n  5. Advance row pointers by pitch values, decrement nHeight\n  6. EMMS to clear MMX state before return\n\nParameters\n  pDest - Destination buffer pointer (output)\n  nDestPitch - Destination row stride in bytes\n  pSrc - Source buffer pointer (input)\n  nSrcPitch - Source row stride in bytes\n  dwWidth - Width in pixels/bytes to process per row\n  nHeight - Number of rows to process\n  byColorKey - Color key value (0x00-0xFF) for transparency test\n  pFallback - Fallback buffer pointer for substitution when color key matches\n\nReturns\n  void (modifies pDest in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases\n  - SIMD optimization: Uses MMX when DetectSIMDCapabilities() >= 2 and dwWidth >= 8\n  - Processes 8 bytes at a time with MMX, then handles 0-7 byte remainder with scalar loop\n  - Requires CPU capability detection via DetectSIMDCapabilities() call\n  - EMMS instruction clears FPU/MMX state to prevent floating-point errors\n  - Handles non-contiguous buffers via pitch parameters (allows for padded rows)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
