      "name": "ConvertRgb24ToRgb16Averaged",
      "signature": "void ConvertRgb24ToRgb16Averaged(ushort * pwDestPixels, byte * pSrcPixels)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts 24-bit RGB pixels to 16-bit RGB555 format with 2x2 block averaging.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Iterate through 256x256 grid (0x300 / 3 = 256 pixels per dimension)\n  2. For each output pixel, read two 24-bit RGB values from source\n  3. Apply mask 0xFEFEFE to clear LSB of each color channel (enables overflow-safe averaging)\n  4. Add the two masked values together (implicit divide-by-2 from cleared LSBs)\n  5. Extract and pack RGB channels into 15-bit format:\n     - Red:   bits 20-23 of combined value -> bits 10-14 of output\n     - Green: bits 9-13 of combined value -> bits 5-9 of output\n     - Blue:  bits 1-5 of combined value -> bits 0-4 of output\n  6. Store 16-bit pixel to destination buffer, advance pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pwDestPixels  Pointer to destination buffer for 16-bit RGB555 pixels\n  pSrcPixels    Pointer to source buffer containing 24-bit RGB data (768 bytes per row)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Processes exactly 256x256 output pixels (65536 total)\n  - Source buffer must contain at least 768 bytes (256 * 3 bytes per pixel)\n  - No bounds checking performed",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:b93e110731ae63b04bb19807b4f1a7b6",
