      "name": "AllocateHeapMemory",
      "signature": "void * AllocateHeapMemory(uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates memory from the application's private heap.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Retrieve the private heap handle from g_hPrivateHeap\n  2. Call HeapAlloc with dwFlags=0x0 (no special allocation flags)\n  3. Return the allocated memory pointer via EAX\n\nParameters:\n  dwSize  Size in bytes to allocate from the private heap\n\nReturns:\n  Success: Pointer to allocated memory block\n  Failure: NULL if allocation fails or heap is exhausted\n\nNotes:\n  Private heap is created elsewhere via HeapCreate with HEAP_NO_SERIALIZE (0x1).\n  Caller is responsible for freeing memory via HeapFree.\n  No zero-initialization (HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY not used).",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
