      "name": "QuickSortPartitionThreeWay",
      "signature": "void QuickSortPartitionThreeWay(byte * pBase, byte * pEnd, int nElemSize, void * pfnCompare)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Quicksort partition subroutine using three-way partitioning.\n  Partitions array into regions based on comparison function.\n  \n  Algorithm:\n    1. Initialize current element pointer (EBX) to first element\n    2. Initialize pivot pointer (EBP) to first element (ESI)\n    3. Loop through array comparing each element via callback:\n       a. Call comparison function for current vs pivot (0x1000bd8d)\n       b. If result > 0, update pivot to current element\n       c. Advance to next element\n    4. Once scan complete, swap pivot with last element\n    5. Update upper bound and repeat partition on remaining range\n  \n  Parameters:\n    pBase (ESP+0x18): Pointer to first element of array\n    pEnd (ESP+0x14): Pointer to last element (exclusive upper bound)\n    elemSize (ESP+0x20): Size of each element in bytes\n    pfnCompare (ESP+0x2c): Pointer to comparison callback function\n  \n  Returns:\n    void\n  \n  Special Cases:\n    - Empty or single-element arrays: returns immediately without partition\n    - Comparison callback expected to return: >0 if first arg > second, <=0 otherwise\n    - In-place partitioning: modifies array during execution via swap() calls",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
