      "name": "CreatePrivateHeap",
      "signature": "void CreatePrivateHeap(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Creates a private heap for module memory allocations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Call HeapCreate with HEAP_NO_SERIALIZE flag (0x1)\n  2. Set initial heap size to 0x1000 (4096) bytes\n  3. Set maximum size to 0 (heap is growable without limit)\n  4. Store returned heap handle in global g_hPrivateHeap\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result stored in global g_hPrivateHeap\n  On success: g_hPrivateHeap contains valid heap handle\n  On failure: g_hPrivateHeap is NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - HEAP_NO_SERIALIZE (0x1) disables mutual exclusion for performance\n  - Should only be used in single-threaded scenarios or with external sync\n  - Called once during InitializeRuntimeEnvironment",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
