      "name": "SetBitInTable",
      "signature": "void SetBitInTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Builds bit table by setting bits for huffman tree nodes\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize ESI to base table address (ESI += 0xd068)\n  2. Right-shift EAX by 0x2 to get entry count\n  3. Loop through entries:\n     - Check if first byte at [ESI] has bit 0x1 set\n     - If not set: advance ESI by 0x4, decrement counter, repeat\n     - If set: extract word at [ESI + 0x2]\n  4. For each set entry: shift and mask bits, OR into output buffer [EDI]\n  5. Process all entries until counter reaches 0\n\nParameters: (implicit register parameters)\n  EAX: Entry count (will be divided by 4 during execution)\n  ESI: Pointer to table of entries to process\n  EDI: Pointer to output bit table buffer\n\nReturns: Nothing (void), modifies output buffer at [EDI]",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
