      "name": "ConvertRgb24ToRgb565",
      "signature": "void ConvertRgb24ToRgb565(ushort * pDest16, byte * pSrc24)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts 256 RGB24 pixels to RGB16 (RGB565) format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Read 3-byte RGB24 pixel (B, G, R order)\n  2. Extract R (bits 7:3), G (bits 7:2), B (bits 7:3)\n  3. Pack into 16-bit: RRRRR GGGGGG BBBBB (RGB565)\n  4. Store to 2-byte destination buffer\n  5. Loop for 0x100 (256) pixels\n\nParameters:\n  pDest16 - Pointer to 16-bit destination pixel buffer (512 bytes)\n  pSrc24  - Pointer to 24-bit source pixel buffer (768 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fixed pixel count of 256 (no bounds checking)\n  - Source buffer must be at least 768 bytes (256 * 3)\n  - Destination buffer must be at least 512 bytes (256 * 2)\n  - Used by Smacker video decoder for frame blitting",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:214d89551dae9843212c24760beae5fa",
